|name3 = Clam Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cinnabar Egg: N206''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Clam Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, reverting to this form may prove useful if a cheaper, more spammable meatshield is needed in an [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] stage.

==='''True Form'''===
Clam Cat attempts to be an [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] for Red and Dark enemies. While its cost is fairly cheap, its base health is mediocre at best, and it has two knockbacks. It does have decent health against them, with 42,840 health ('''53,550''' with [[Fruit Treasures]]), but since it has two knockbacks, it can effectively only take half of those numbers before being pushed back. If you want to use it as intended, it will require heavy boosting, as it reaches an impressive 100,800 health at Lv.50+10, which is pretty good. Also, because it has a somewhat-long 5.87 second recharge, using Research [[Cat Combo]]s with it is highly recommended.

Against Behemoths in general, bringing Clam Cat is not the best idea. It only reaches 17,850 health (33,600 health at Lv.50+10) against them, which will be shredded in seconds by threats like [[Wild Doge]], [[Pterowl Hazuku]] and more. This is not the case against Red or Dark Behemoths, though, as the multipliers from Behemoth Slayer and Resistant stack to up to '''89,250''' health at Lv.30, and '''168,000''' at Lv.50+10!

Much like [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Tank Cat]], Clam Cat's 100 range can be used to [[cheese]] few stages where the boss spawns on base hit and there are infinitely respawning weak peons. While Li'l Tank Cat has higher health than Clam Cat if fully boosted and Talented, Clam Cat has much higher damage and DPS, meaning that it can destroy the base faster than Li'l Tank Cat can (though that may be a double-edged sword when trying to cheese).

